  "articleBody": "It's frustrating when you see your bathroom drywall looking rough, isn't it? Often, recurring damage, especially in a bathroom, points to an underlying issue that a quick patch won't fix. The most common culprit is moisture. Bathrooms are naturally humid spaces, but persistent water intrusion from a leaky pipe, a poorly sealed shower, or even just inadequate ventilation can wreak havoc on standard drywall. If you're noticing bubbling, soft spots, discoloration, or even mold growth, these are all big red flags. Cosmetic repairs might hide the problem temporarily, but the moisture source needs to be addressed first. Otherwise, you're just signing up for repeat repairs and potentially bigger issues down the line. We typically see situations where the initial water problem was ignored, leading to more extensive drywall deterioration than initially visible. Getting to the root cause of the moisture is the very first step, and often the most crucial one, before any drywall work begins. Don't let a small leak turn into a major headache!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}